   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "145cf46c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 3. An ARX model for the heating of a box"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "920859e2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The final part is about identifying a suitable ARX model for predicting the hourly heating of a test\n",
    "box (a small building). The box has a window in the south facing wall.\n",
    "\n",
    "In an experiment times series were recorded of the variables:\n",
    "- $P_h$ (*Ph* in data) the heat from electrical heaters (W).\n",
    "- $T_{delta}$ (*Tdelta* in data) the difference between the internal and external temperature (◦C)\n",
    "- $G_v$ (*Gv* in data) the vertical solar radiation onto the box side with a window (W/m2)\n",
    "\n",
    "The data consists of average hourly values – in total 231 hours. It’s available in the *box_data_60min.csv*\n",
    "file.\n",
    "\n",
    "In the experiment the internal air temperature was kept constant with a thermostatic control of the\n",
    "heating – hence the heating change depending on the weather conditions.\n",
    "\n",
    "The objective is to find a suitable model, which makes good predictions of the heating.\n",
    "\n",
    "Lags have been generated and included in the data with a naming syntax such that, e.g.: *Ph.l1* is the\n",
    "heating lagged one step, *Ph.l2* is heating lagged two steps and so fourth."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 49,
   "id": "ca14485b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "15f1c0a3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
